==========================
Code Craft AI Interfaces
==========================

The ``codecraftai-interfaces`` package is the shared contract layer for the ccai suite. It is intentionally dependency-light and contains only abstract interfaces and small protocol classes that other ``codecraftai-*`` packages implement or depend on, keeping those packages from having to import each other directly for the sake of a type hint.

Highlights
==========

- ``ICommandRunner`` and ``IFileOperator`` for command execution and file manipulation (local or over SSH).
- ``IBasicCredential`` for credential abstractions used by ``codecraftai-credentials``.
- ``IIncludeFilter`` and ``IExcludeFilter`` for generic filtering.
- ``ISerializable`` for objects that participate in configuration or result streams.
- ``ITestJob`` for test-job integration points and ``IHint`` for pluggable hint metadata.

Repository Structure
====================

- ``development/`` - Runtime environment scripts.
- ``repository-setup/`` - Repository homing and setup scripts.
- ``source/packages/`` - Package source code.
- ``specs/`` - Requirements, design, and task documentation.
- ``userguide/`` - Standards, conventions, and documentation.

Environment Setup
=================

When working in a Codex container:

.. code-block:: bash

   ./development/setup-agent-container

For local development:

.. code-block:: bash

   ./repository-setup/rehome-repository
   ./development/setup-environment

Running Tests
=============

Activate the virtual environment:

.. code-block:: bash

   source .venv/bin/activate

Run ``unittest`` tests:

.. code-block:: bash

   python -m unittest discover -s source/tests -p "test_*.py"

